  "headline": "Serang Regent Confirms BPJS Aid For PT Fonusa Agung Mulia Victims",
  "seoTitle": "PT Fonusa Agung Mulia Fire Victims",
  "metaDescription": "Serang Regent Ratu Rachmatuzakiyah states workers affected by the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia factory fire will receive BPJS Ketenagakerjaan compensation.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Serang Regent Ratu Rachmatuzakiyah pledged BPJS Ketenagakerjaan financial and medical assistance for all factory fire victims.",
    "Authorities have recovered 24 body bags from the site, with identification processes expected to take two to three weeks.",
    "Search and rescue efforts remain ongoing as officials work to locate approximately 50 individuals reported missing following the incident."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire occurred at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory located in Cikande, Serang. The disaster has drawn significant attention due to the high number of casualties, with regional officials coordinating the emergency response. Local authorities, including the Banten Police and provincial leadership, are overseeing the evacuation and identification of victims, noting that two recovered bodies were found in an embrace. While 24 body bags have been transported to the Bhayangkara Hospital for forensic analysis, current reports indicate that roughly 50 people remain missing. The Serang Regent, Ratu Rachmatuzakiyah, has confirmed that all affected workers will be provided with social security coverage and medical care through BPJS Ketenagakerjaan. Identification efforts are complex and officials estimate that determining the identities of all victims may require two to three weeks of forensic work.",
